Incudela (the operating system) is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE).
Cuditor (the language: compiler, assembler, linker, standard library and language tools) is licensed
under the MIT License (LICENSE-MIT).

Copyright 2026 Kyle Curtis.

Which license applies to a path is recorded in REUSE.toml (REUSE specification 3.2, SPDX identifiers);
an SPDX-License-Identifier line inside a file, where present, wins. In short:

  Apache-2.0  examples/kernel, examples/efi, examples/user, examples/modules, examples/apps,
              tools that build, seal or partition OS images (tools/cudseal*, tools/incudela-part*,
              tools/krel*, tools/mkfont*, tools/ostools.cud, tools/repro-*, tools/busybox,
              tools/ed25519*, tools/espmigrate*), tests/os, tests/dwarf and the tests of those tools
  MIT         everything else: selfhost/, std/, seed/, src/ (the Rust bootstrap), tools/fas, fld,
              fmt, lsp, pkg, embed, c2cud, bench, provenance, the fuzzers, bench/, the compiler's
              tests, build.sh, run_tests.sh, ./cuditor and the docs

Not covered by either license: third-party sources that the build downloads and verifies but does
not vendor, such as BusyBox (GPL-2.0) and CPython (PSF-2.0).
